Mijovia skin

Mijovia is a community wiki skin derived from MediaWiki’s Example scaffold.
Its community navigation is configured at MediaWiki:Mijovia-wiki-navigation.
Special:MijoviaThemeDesigner publishes themes to MediaWiki:Mijovia-theme.json.

The code is released into public domain, which means you can freely copy it,
modify and release as your own skin without providing attribution and with
absolutely no restrictions. Remember to change the license information if you
do not intend to provide your changes on the same terms.

See <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> for full licensing
details.


Fandom Desktop reference
------------------------

The skin templates follow the Earferana Wiki browser capture in the workspace
fandom_reference directory. fandom-desktop.css contains rules extracted from
the capture's load_002_QID9.css, plus its inline edit-font and collapsible rules.
fandom-theme.css contains the captured Earferana theme declarations and the
light navigation palette from the saved light desktop stylesheet. The
ResourceLoader module loads them in this skin only. Integration overrides are
in skin.css. The original Fandom styles and icon artwork are third-party
reference material. The CC0 notice above applies to the Example scaffold and
does not grant a license to Fandom's material or Earferana's artwork.

The wiki can set its logo and light and dark banners through Theme Designer.
The community header uses the configured wiki icon by default. The four Latin Rubik
WOFF2 files come from the original stylesheet's public Fandom CDN URLs.
See resources/fonts/OFL.txt for Rubik's license.

For a screenshot fixture on the local development Test Wiki, create the Home
page with fixtures/Home.wiki. From the workspace root:

  docker compose exec -T php php maintenance/run.php edit --wiki=testwiki --createonly Home < mediawiki/skins/Mijovia/fixtures/Home.wiki

The fixture supplies the article body. For a visual comparison, use the saved
capture's site title, community logo, page count, and three menu headings as
fixture data. The live skin continues to use the local wiki's values.

Signed-in Acepogland preview
---------------------------

The signed-in article layout uses the saved Acepogland browser capture. On
Test Wiki, the existing imported article needs PortableInfobox, the three
images in fixtures/acepogland-images, and the local compatibility versions of
Template:Rewrite, Template:Main, and Template:Country About in fixtures.
Upload the images under their existing filenames. The article text and
category membership are supplied by the imported page.
